-- Plan 99 wave 1. The SOLVE stage doc 88 §1 adds to the pipeline, reporting
-- against the `.vlt` the author wrote rather than against generated Rust.
--
-- The body says `bool` and the signature says `u64`, so Lattice's constraint
-- store becomes unsatisfiable. `VLT1004` names the conflicting types and the
-- reason that created the constraint, and points at `voltaic sig --why` for the
-- chain behind it.
--
-- It is a **warning in the lint band**, not an error, and that is doc 86 §2's
-- first corollary rather than timidity: rustc is the authority on types, so
-- Lattice advises and rustc decides. Row 101 owns the `VLT07xx` ranges and will
-- re-site it there.
--
-- This is a lint case rather than a UI case because it has to *build*:
-- `code_coverage.rs` records that the two corpora assert opposite things, and a
-- warning has no home in the one that requires rejection.

wrong : u64
wrong = true
